note right of main_py #FFFBEB
  **UNAUTHENTICATED + UNBOUNDED**
  · POST /chat and GET /reports* declare no auth
    dependency (main.py:274-275, :257-271); the file
    says so at main.py:55-56. auth.current_user()
    never returns None (auth.py:89-92), so every
    ownership branch is dead-on-the-false-side.
  · Only CORSMiddleware is installed (main.py:47-53):
    no request-size limit — ChatRequest.image / .pdf
    are unbounded base64 (main.py:187-197).
  · Catch-all at main.py:670-672 publishes raw
    str(exc) to the browser; nothing is logged.
  · No wall-clock budget on worker() (main.py:383-677).
    The only bound is LLM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT = 300 s
    (config.py:264 -> llm.py:78).
  · lifespan has no shutdown branch (main.py:27-38):
    _live_generations and _background_tasks are never
    drained on SIGTERM.
end note

note bottom of e_router #FFFBEB
  **SWALLOWED CLASSIFIER FAILURE — 600 s worst case**
  Two bare `except Exception: pass` (router.py:121-122,
  :130-131) hide connection-refused, 400 window errors
  and timeouts identically; nothing is logged anywhere
  in the file. A wedged vllm-router **plus** a wedged
  vllm costs 2 × 300 s before the unconditional
  `return "rag"` (router.py:133) — a total classifier
  outage silently sends greetings into vector search.
  There is no confidence score, threshold or logprob.
end note

note bottom of e_orch #FFFBEB
  **ON THE CRITICAL PATH OF EVERY TEXT TURN**
  orchestrate.decide has no timeout (orchestrate.py:138)
  and runs at main.py:412 — BEFORE the first `status`
  event at main.py:415. Two swallow-everything handlers
  (:104-106, :142-144) make "endpoint dead" and "prompt
  too long" both read as "do neither". `_JSON_RE` is
  greedy `\{.*\}` (:38) with no <think>/fence stripping.
end note

note right of e_agent #FFFBEB
  **NO TIMEOUT, NO CANCELLATION, RAW ERRORS TO THE UI**
  · asyncio.gather at agent.py:405 has no
    return_exceptions=True — a CancelledError on Stop
    aborts the gather and leaves siblings running.
  · Per-step catch-all (agent.py:387-398) ships
    str(exc)[:200] to the browser as step.detail.
  · Worst case: plan 2×300 s + ceil(8/3) waves +
    synthesis, > 20 min, uncancellable (agent.py:397-400).
  · agent.py:312-335 is 24 lines of UNREACHABLE duplicate
    Salesforce branch (identical guard at :288).
  · The `web` gate is applied only at plan time;
    execute_steps never sees it (agent.py:571-580).
end note

note right of c_guard #DC2626
  **GUARD IS ONE BYPASS DEEP** (reproduced)
  `_scan` does not model DuckDB `E'…'` escape strings,
  so `SELECT E'\'' , 1 ; DROP TABLE accounts` desyncs
  `cleaned` from `bare` and defeats BOTH the stacked-
  statement check (sql_guard.py:142) and the keyword
  blocklist (:146) in one input. Replacement scans
  (`FROM '/etc/passwd'`), quoted function names
  (`"read_text"(…)`) and `duckdb_*` / `pragma_*`
  metadata functions also pass.
  What actually saves the system is NOT this module —
  it is the DuckDB lockdown at sql.py:124-132
  (read_only=True, enable_external_access=False,
  autoinstall/autoload extensions=False).
end note

note right of c_net #DC2626
  **SSRF: CORRECT, WITH TWO HOLES**
  Blocked and verified: file:/gopher:/ftp:, IPv4 and
  IPv6 private/loopback/link-local/reserved, decimal
  and octal encodings, userinfo spoofing, multi-A
  rebinding, redirect into private space, >3 hops.
  NOT blocked:
  · TOCTOU — resolve_public_ips returns validated IPs
    and assert_url_is_fetchable throws them away
    (net.py:87,:99); httpx re-resolves at connect
    (:137). Nothing pins the address.
  · 100.64.0.0/10 (CGNAT / Tailscale) is fetchable —
    is_private is False on Python 3.12.
  · No destination-port restriction, no total deadline,
    no retry/circuit breaker; getaddrinfo (:76) has no
    timeout and parks a thread-pool worker.
  Reached ONLY from search.py:313 and url.py:34 —
  core/repo.py:137 (api.github.com) bypasses it.
end note

note bottom of e_sql #FFFBEB
  **THE EVENT LOOP STALLS HERE**
  `_execute` is a plain `def` (sql.py:117) called from
  an async function at :201 and :206, so the DuckDB
  query — and every export of up to 100 000 rows
  (:408) — runs on the single shared event loop and
  stalls **all** concurrent SSE streams (one uvicorn
  worker, orchestrator/Dockerfile:52).
  The blanket `except Exception` at sql.py:203 treats a
  dead vllm endpoint exactly like bad SQL and spends a
  second LLM call re-prompting; the retry's output is
  never re-checked by references_a_known_table (:193).
end note

note bottom of c_schema #FFFBEB
  **STALE SCHEMA, DEAD KNOB**
  invalidate() (schema_cache.py:27-31) has no caller, so
  a table the sync-worker just created is invisible to
  the SQL-writing model for up to the hard-coded 300 s
  TTL (:74). SCHEMA_CACHE_TTL is read at config.py:265
  and never consumed. get() returns the cached dict BY
  REFERENCE (:22) — a mutating caller corrupts it for
  every later request.
end note

note bottom of c_sf #FFFBEB
  **LIVE PRODUCTION ORG, NO QUOTA**
  live_sf._object_hint() calls `schema_cache()` — the
  SchemaCache *instance*, which defines no `__call__` —
  so it always raises TypeError, swallowed at
  live_sf.py:57-58. The SOQL prompt therefore NEVER
  receives the org-object context it was written to
  carry. `history` is accepted by write_soql (:61) and
  fetch_live (:141) and never used.
  core/salesforce.py:108 holds the token in an unlocked
  module global; only one 401 re-auth, no rate limit,
  no circuit breaker, no per-user quota.
end note

note bottom of c_chart #FFFBEB
  **SILENT CHART LOSS + A STREAM STALL**
  build_chart's blanket `except Exception`
  (chart_pipeline.py:115-117) turns every internal
  defect into "no chart" plus one WARNING line.
  `ask_model` has no timeout at this layer, and
  attach_chart is awaited at sql.py:426 BEFORE the
  narrative stream starts at :428 — a hung model call
  stalls the whole /chat SSE response.
  Good news: chart_prompt (:49-76) serialises only
  aggregate column metadata, so no Salesforce cell
  value ever reaches the chart model.
end note

note bottom of e_ds #FFFBEB
  **PROMPT-INJECTION ASYMMETRY**
  dataset.py is the ONLY engine that fences retrieved
  content as untrusted (DATA_START/DATA_END,
  dataset.py:27-28,:40-45,:71). Fetched web-page bodies
  (search.py:374-378), pasted-page text (url.py:63) and
  Salesforce record text from LanceDB (rag.py:105-112)
  are pasted raw into the user turn with no delimiter.
  Worse, main.py:502-510 re-injects stored page text as
  a **system** message, and engines/__init__.py:16-19
  keeps every system message forever.
end note

note bottom of e_report #FFFBEB
  **UNBOUNDED SUBPROCESS, LOST ARTEFACTS**
  _run_pandoc awaits communicate() with NO timeout
  (report.py:117). The two conversions at :257-258 are
  unguarded: if .docx succeeds and .pdf fails (missing
  weasyprint/pandoc) the RuntimeError escapes, the turn
  ends in an `error` event and report_files is never
  emitted even though the .docx exists on disk.
  Two reports with the same title in the same second
  share a base_name and silently overwrite (:228).
end note

